---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import profile from '../assets/brand/profile.png';
import { CATEGORIES, SERIES } from '../data/categories';
---

<Base title="About" description="VidyalAI publishes clear, sourced explainers on how to build real systems with large language models.">
  <div class="container-narrow about">
    <header class="page-head about-head">
      <Image src={profile} alt="VidyalAI logo: an open book with glowing pixels rising from its pages." width={160} height={160} class="about-logo" />
      <div>
        <h1>About VidyalAI</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Knowledge amplified</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        VidyalAI is a learning resource for engineers who build with large language models. The goal is simple:
        explain how real systems work, clearly enough to act on and with sources you can check.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first collection is the <a href="/series/llm-system-design/">{SERIES.name}</a> series: 25 deep dives on the
        problems that come up when an LLM feature moves from demo to production. Each article follows the same
        shape, so you can find what you need quickly:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>TL;DR:</strong> the answer in one paragraph.</li>
        <li><strong>Requirements to pin down first:</strong> the questions that change the design.</li>
        <li><strong>The design:</strong> components, numbers and worked examples.</li>
        <li><strong>How to measure it:</strong> metrics, targets and evals.</li>
        <li><strong>Tradeoffs</strong> and <strong>common mistakes</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Further reading:</strong> the papers and docs behind each claim.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Topics</h2>
      <ul>
        {CATEGORIES.map((c) => <li><a href={`/category/${c.slug}/`}>{c.name}</a>: {c.blurb}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Numbers, prices and model names in this field go stale quickly. Each article cites its sources so you can check
        them. If you spot something wrong or out of date, please let us know so it can be fixed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .about-head h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .about-logo {
    width: 120px;
    height: 120px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: 0 0 40px -10px var(--accent);
  }
  .tagline {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0 !important;
    font-size: 0.85rem !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent) !important;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
